<DocsLayout title="Creating installation media">
    <h1>Creating installation media</h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        Write the Octlitch ISO to a USB drive before booting the installer.
    </p>

    <h2>Before you begin</h2>

    <p>
        You will need an Octlitch ISO image and a USB drive with at least
        8 GB of capacity.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-note">
        <strong>Warning</strong>

        <p>
            Writing the ISO will erase the contents of the selected USB
            drive. Back up anything important before continuing.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Verify the ISO</h2>

    <p>
        Each Octlitch release provides a SHA256 checksum on the download
        page.
    </p>

    <p>
        On Linux, verify the ISO with:
    </p>

    <pre><code>sha256sum Octlitch-*.iso</code></pre>

    <p>
        Compare the result with the checksum published on the Octlitch
        download page.
    </p>

    <h2>Write the ISO</h2>

    <p>
        Use an image-writing utility that writes the ISO directly to the
        USB device like Balena Etcher, Ventoy or Rufus if you are on Windows.
    </p>

    <p>
        Do not extract the ISO contents onto the USB drive as ordinary
        files.
    </p>

    <h3>Using Fedora Media Writer</h3>

    <p>
        Select the option for a custom ISO image, choose the Octlitch ISO,
        select the correct USB drive and begin writing.
    </p>

    <h3>Using the command line</h3>

    <p>
        Advanced Linux users can write the image directly with
        <code>dd</code>.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-note">
        <strong>Check the device carefully</strong>

        <p>
            The following command overwrites the selected device. Replace
            <code>/dev/sdX</code> with the USB device itself, not a
            partition such as <code>/dev/sdX1</code>.
        </p>
    </div>

    <pre><code>sudo dd if=Octlitch-1.0-Alpha-1.iso of=/dev/sdX bs=4M status=progress oflag=sync</code></pre>

    <h2>Boot from the USB</h2>

    <p>
        Restart the computer and open its firmware boot menu. Select the
        USB drive and Octlitch should display its boot menu.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-next">
        <a href="/documentation/installation/">
            Next: Installing Octlitch →
        </a>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
